cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Crypto Orchestra: a multi-agent crypto research and paper-trading system"
message: "If you reference this work, please cite it as below. Please also cite the finding, not just the code: the strategy is documented as unprofitable."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Tei
    given-names: Vitaliy
repository-code: "https://github.com/Vito-bc/crypto-orchestra"
url: "https://github.com/Vito-bc/crypto-orchestra"
abstract: >-
  A multi-agent trading system in which seven specialist LLM sub-agents run
  through a bounded worker pool, an orchestrator weighs their votes, and a
  deterministic risk engine gates the resulting order. The repository is
  primarily a research artifact: its registered headline results are
  byte-identical regenerations from a pinned interpreter, pinned
  result-determining libraries, content-addressed code and a window-scoped
  logical input hash, verified in CI. Its headline
  result is negative — the frozen momentum mechanism shows no positive
  expectancy (profit factor 0.761 over 114 trades on the continuous ZEC-USD
  window, 2021-06-26 to 2026-07-12) — and the repository documents the
  retraction history of several earlier, more favourable claims, including a
  walk-forward harness whose results were void and a regime filter that was
  retired after integrated enforcement made results worse.
keywords:
  - algorithmic-trading
  - paper-trading
  - reproducible-research
  - multi-agent-systems
  - llm-agents
  - backtesting
  - risk-management
  - pre-registration
